# LingoPrep System Grounding Rules

## Project Definition
LingoPrep is an AI-powered English proficiency evaluator specializing in IELTS and TOEFL preparation[cite: 1].

## Technical Stack Architecture
- Frontend: Next.js, Tailwind CSS (inside /lingoprep-frontend)[cite: 1].
- Backend: FastAPI (Python 3.11+) (inside /lingoprep-backend)[cite: 1].
- Database: Supabase PostgreSQL[cite: 1].
- Core LLM Engine: Llama 3 via Ollama/Groq[cite: 1].

## Current Phase Focus (7th Semester Evaluation - 50% Completeness)
We are strictly focused on establishing the objective core engines and baseline data pathways. 
DO NOT write code for Speech-to-Text (Whisper), real-time interactive examiner speech loops, or vector databases yet[cite: 1].

### Target Deliverables for Current Sprints:
1. Supabase database schema for users, session logs, and question banks[cite: 1].
2. Automated Reading Module (MCQ engine)[cite: 1].
3. Automated Listening Module (Audio player + MCQ engine)[cite: 1].
4. Baseline Text Essay Writing Evaluator backend endpoint connected to Llama 3[cite: 1]. 
